  "articleBody": "It’s a bummer when your garage drywall gets damaged, but don't sweat it too much – it's a pretty common issue! The first thing you need to do is figure out what caused the damage. Was it a stray baseball, a car door, or something more serious like a leak? If there's water damage, you absolutely have to find and fix the source of the leak before you even think about patching. Patching over an active leak is just asking for more trouble down the road! Once the cause is sorted, you'll need to assess if it's a small patch job or if an entire panel needs replacing. This also includes looking for hidden damage around the original spot, like near doors, windows, or corners, because sometimes damage isn't as localized as it first appears. When it comes to the repair itself, remember that thin coats of mud are key to avoiding ridges and shrinkage. And getting that repair to blend seamlessly with your existing finish can be trickier than it looks! If the damage is extensive, recurring, or you want a flawless finish, bringing in a pro like HH Remodeling LLC in Aurora is a smart move. We serve the entire Denver area, including Highlands Ranch, Parker, and Arvada, and we can make your garage walls look new again. Call us at 303-505-0866 for a helping hand!",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
